<!--Post: 755--><!--Time: 1092494934-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST755"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 7:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->June 6, 1987: Hattie Smith, 54, was found dead by her husband when he returned to the couple&#39;s home at 3193 S. Clifton. Her nude body was bound hand and foot with materials that came from the house. Police said she was beaten, strangled and drowned in the bathtub. There were no signs of forced entry. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 755-->
<!--Post: 7825--><!--Time: 1108693847-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7825"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 6:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting.  I wonder if there is any other information on this case.  We have here several warning bells.  The victim&#39;s house had no sign of forced entry, which is simialr to other cases of the BTK&#39;s ...  <BR> <BR>The victim was Bound &#40;hands and feet&#41;, Tortured &#40;strangled and drowned&#41;, and Killed.  Which is the consistant theme between all of BTK&#39;s murders. <BR> <BR>Is there any other information that Wichitan posters out there can gather on this case?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7825-->
<!--Post: 9459--><!--Time: 1109535280-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9459"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 12:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;3193 S  Clifton, age 54. Her nude body, bound hand and foot, was  found by her  husband when he returned home after work at 3:45. She was beaten,  strangled by hand, and drowned in the bath tub. There was  no sign of  forced entry. The house was surrounded by a cyclone fence and  shielded from 31st St. by a high wooden fence. The large  family dog was in  the fenced in back yard when her husband got home, and  the house  showed signs that she had fought for her life. The house  had been ransacked  and some items were missing. The back door was unlocked.&#34; <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9459-->
<!--Post: 9460--><!--Time: 1109535380-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9460"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 12:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->She was bound!  Tortured by strangulation and drowinging!  Then Killed ... <BR> <BR>The dog was put in the fenced in backyard!!!!!! <BR> <BR>And Items were missing!!!! O.o<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9460-->
<!--Post: 9876--><!--Time: 1109680005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9876"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 4:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Where&#39;s the lovable &#34;map dude&#34;  where is Hattie Smith&#39;s home in relation to other BTK cases?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9876-->
<!--Post: 10961--><!--Time: 1110319774-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10961"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Km<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Km<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 2:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have always thought that Hattie Smith was a BTK victim from all the similarities.  Another thing I find interesting is that both she and Deanna Law were found in the bathtub.  I think he did both murders.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
